UU Remote Ubuntu Bridge installer package (experimental fork)
=============================================================

This is a source/installer bundle, not a ready-to-use UU Linux host. The original
Wine/Xvfb, RDP/VNC, input-broker, and maintenance architecture is by Lachlan
Chen; this fork contains work-in-progress host-specific changes. The original
MIT license and attribution are included.

This fork primarily targets x86-64 Ubuntu 26.04 GNOME. Ubuntu 24.04 remains
supported as the upstream baseline. In the download directory, run:

    sudo apt install ./uu-remote-ubuntu-bridge-installer_0.3.0-rc3-1_amd64.deb

Then open "UU Remote Setup" from the app menu and keep its terminal window
open until setup finishes. The same menu slot becomes "UU Remote" after setup.
If the setup icon is unavailable, run `uu-remote-bridge-setup` from a desktop
terminal instead.

Run setup as the logged-in desktop user, not with sudo. It copies
the reviewed source to a versioned user-writable directory before building;
the .deb installation itself does not download software, alter the desktop,
configure unattended access, or log into UU. The setup command may request
sudo for Ubuntu/WineHQ dependencies, downloads the hash-verified official UU
installer, and asks for normal UU account sign-in. It does not include or
redistribute NetEase's proprietary programs.

After setup, use the single "UU Remote" desktop entry for managing this Ubuntu
host and experimental control of another computer. It follows UU's active
session window as the window changes size. Matching old Wine/bridge shortcuts
are archived under ~/.local/share/uu-remote-bridge/old-shortcuts/. The advanced
fallback `uu-remote control` explicitly asks before pausing the host bridge,
opens the official UU client through Wine on the visible desktop, and restores
the host service on exit. Do not confirm that fallback over a UU session to
this same Ubuntu machine, or you will disconnect yourself.

The bundled source is a release snapshot, not a Git checkout. The project's
Git-based automatic updater/upgrade workflow is not supported from this .deb;
use a real source checkout for that workflow. To undo the bridge before
removing the package, run `uu-remote-bridge-setup --uninstall` as the desktop
user. Removing the Debian package alone deliberately leaves per-user UU state
untouched. The 26.04 controller path and UU 4.41 remain experimental; do not
treat the package as a broadly validated compatibility claim. Upgrading the
.deb does not automatically rerun setup: run `uu-remote-bridge-setup` again
from a logged-in desktop terminal after an upgrade.

Source and issue tracker: https://github.com/cnsunfishegg/uu-remote-ubuntu-bridge
Original project: https://github.com/lachlanchen/uu-remote-ubuntu-bridge
